<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anawrahta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1014–1077</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Anawrahta Minsaw</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anawrahta was king of Pagan from 1044 to 1077 and is regarded as the founder of the first Burmese empire. He conquered the Mon kingdom of Thaton in 1057, brought much of present-day Myanmar under one rule, extended irrigation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyaukse">Kyaukse</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> lands and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theravada-buddhism">Theravada Buddhism</a>, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shwezigon-pagoda">Shwezigon Pagoda</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anawrahta.jpg" alt="Anawrahta" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Phyo WP · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anawrahta_at_National_museum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
